# Build context for both images (they are built from the repository root, so
# this one file governs each).
#
# Excluding build output is not only about size: a bin/ or node_modules/ copied
# in from a developer's Mac would shadow what the image builds for linux and
# produce an image that runs locally and nowhere else.

**/bin/
**/obj/
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/.angular/

.git/
.github/
.vscode/
.claude/
**/.DS_Store

# Nothing in the images needs the docs or the local compose file.
*.md
docker-compose*.yml

# Local overrides and anything secret-shaped. Real configuration reaches a
# container through environment variables, never through a copied file.
#
# appsettings.Development.json is excluded deliberately: it is safe in the
# repository because it only points at containers on one machine, but it also
# carries the local seed-admin password, and a published image has no business
# containing any credential at all.
**/appsettings.Development.json
**/appsettings.Development.json.local
**/secrets.json
**/.env
**/*.env

**/TestResults/
**/publish/
